Ids are F1, F2, F3... in severity order, highest first.

"read" is every source file you opened to reason about this diff, paths relative to the
tree — including files you opened and cleared. It is the record that this review actually
read source: a result with no findings and nothing read is discarded as a run that reviewed
nothing.

If you find nothing, write {"findings":[],"read":[...]} — an empty findings list is a
legitimate and useful result, as long as the read list is truthful. Do not pad either list.

severity: high = data loss, auth bypass, or breakage hitting every user of the path.
medium = wrong behaviour under conditions that occur in normal use.
low = real but narrow, or requires an unusual configuration.

